exports[`security.habitat.redteam (contract renders) given: [case6] apply scaffolds + hands off honestly when no route is bound when: [t0] apply runs with no bound route then: it reaches the handoff (exit 0) and matches snapshot (date masked) 1`] = `
"🐈 chartin course...

🧿 security.habitat.redteam --scope . --grain exfil --peers 3 --budget 1
   ├─ scope: .
   ├─ grains: exfil  (1 partition(s), disjoint by grain-surface)
   ├─ peers: 3 per grain-partition  ⇒ 3 blind peers total
   ├─ budget: 1 loop cycle(s) — each draws one detect → verify → repair pass
   ├─ projected: 3 peers × 1 cycle(s) = up to 3 peer-dispatch runs
   ├─ the ward loop: ground → detect → verify → repair → promote → (loop | terminate)
   └─ per-grain prompts (each peer is blind to the others' slice + theory)
      ├─ exfil — "by what channel could data leave this slice — net, DNS, log, webhook?"
      └─ each claim = a chain (entry/exit → mechanism → blast radius|audience), keyed on channel+mechanism

🐈 anchors away!

🧿 security.habitat.redteam --mode apply
   ├─ route: .behavior/v<date>.guardian-redteam.grain=exfil/ (scaffolded, NOT bound)
   ├─ the ward loop runs through the route stones (blind peers are agent work):
   │  ├─ 1.ground   — map the focus-surface per grain
   │  ├─ 2.detect   — dispatch blind peers, fan claims in (keyed channel+mechanism)
   │  ├─ 3.verify   — confirm vs tree, classify, sort by permanence trigger
   │  ├─ 4.repair   — gated, disposition-aware, PENDING-REDETECT until confirmed
   │  └─ 5.promote  — teach the kin (fullsun-safe), then loop or terminate
   ├─ ⚠️ the route is NOT bound — bind it before you drive:
   │  └─ rhx route.bind.set --route .behavior/v<date>.guardian-redteam.grain=exfil/
   └─ then drive it: rhx route.drive

   ⚠️ informational only — NOT professional security advice. analyses are
      not exhaustive; consult a qualified security professional for any
      assessment of your own habitat.
"
`;

